The system should cite evidence in the final JSON output by including a "References" or "Sources" field that lists the relevant documents and their corresponding page numbers (e.g., [ART2554_lit_2025_MHRA_Evaluating_Hallu_p01_c001] 2025_MHRA_Evaluating_Hallucinations_in_AI_for_Healthcare_Reg (part 20/27) (p.1)). This allows clinicians to easily access the underlying evidence and verify the accuracy of the AI-generated responses.

Example:

"References": [
{
"Document": "[ART2554_lit_2025_MHRA_Evaluating_Hallu_p01_c001]",
"Page Number": "1"
},
{
"Document": "[DOC003_2020_Rudin_Interpretability_of_ML_Predic_p04_c008]",
"Page Number": "4"
}
]

Note that the system should only include references that are directly relevant to the AI-generated response and not include unnecessary or redundant information.
